# HTML images

  An `<img>` tag on a line of its own is shown
  like a Markdown image:

  [image: Icon]

  So is an image wrapped the way READMEs
  centre a logo; kiri does not centre it:

  [image: Test pattern]

  A `<picture>` shows its `<img>`, whatever
  its sources say:

  [image: Transparent in a picture]

  A linked image is shown, but cannot be
  clicked yet:

  [image: Linked icon] <https://example.com>

  In running text, [image: Fish & chips] stays
  alt text, as Markdown images do, and a
  linked [image: icon] <https://example.com>
  is a link.

  A missing file shows its alt text:

  [image: Missing image]

  These stay HTML source: a block with text, a
  block with two images and an `<img>` without
  a `src`.

  <p>Text and <img src="images/icon.png" alt="an icon"></p>

  <p><img src="images/icon.png" alt="One"><img src="images/icon.png" alt="Two"></p>

  <img alt="No source">
